{
  "description": "Shared origin rule cases for createBridge's allowedOrigins validation and for every origin matcher (the page client, OriginRules.swift). Rules follow Android's addWebMessageListener origin rules, narrowed to what every platform can match: `*` (any origin, opaque ones included), `http(s)://host[:port]`, `http(s)://*.host[:port]` (subdomains only, not host itself) or an IP literal (`https://127.0.0.1`, `https://[::1]:99`). Hosts are ASCII (punycode for IDNs); no path, trailing slash, userinfo, query or custom scheme. Scheme and host compare case-insensitively; a missing port is 80 for http and 443 for https, on rules and origins alike. A rule createBridge rejects matches nothing. `validation`: whether createBridge accepts the rule. `cases`: whether a page with `origin` (location.origin form) matches any of `rules`.",
  "validation": [
    {
      "rule": "*",
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "rule": "https://example.com",
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "rule": "http://localhost:8090",
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "rule": "https://*.example.com",
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "rule": "https://*.example.com:8443",
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "rule": "HTTPS://Example.COM",
      "valid": true
    },
    {
